Analysis: Which columns have little impact on employee retention?
The following input columns appear to have no statistically significant
correlation with poor outcomes and could potentially be dropped:
 - attrition
 - businessTravel
 - DailyRate
 - department
 - DistanceFromHome
 - Education
 - educationField
 - EmployeeCount
 - EmployeeNumber
 - EnvironmentSatisfaction
 - gender
 - HourlyRate
 - JobInvolvement
 - JobSatisfaction
 - maritalStatus
 - MonthlyRate
 - NumCompaniesWorked
 - over18
 - overTime
 - PercentSalaryHike
 - PerformanceRating
 - RelationshipSatisfaction
 - StandardHours
 - StockOptionLevel
 - TrainingTimesLastYear
 - WorkLifeBalance

Methodology: We compared the distribution of input values between the
worst 25% of performers and the rest of the workforce. Columns where
the distributions were statistically indistinguishable were flagged.

